/K [3]
>>
endobj
233 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Meet my younger self, in my early days in the corporate world, I believed that my hard work and achievements would naturally pave the way for my career progression. I dedicated myself tirelessly to not only meeting but exceeding every target, confident that these accomplishments would secure my promotion. Alongside my primary duties, I undertook a significant side project that ultimately saved the company millions, this came with accolades and recognition that shot my confidence through the roof.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
234 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (However, my confidence turned to despair during my end-of-year review. Despite my hard work and tangible contributions, I was told I wasn't ready for the next step, receiving vague feedback that left me feeling confused and no longer sure of my abilities. Meanwhile, a colleague with seemingly lesser achievements and experience was celebrating his promotion.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
235 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This experience was my first run in with the Excellence Paradox, a lesson that reshaped my understanding of success in the corporate landscape. It highlighted the complex dynamics of climbing the corporate ladder, particularly the importance of visibility, strategic networking, and the political nature of workplaces)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
